            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "You've just linked the schema, you haven't linked where or why this was needed, or the change to the spec that says \"all fan sensors shall be percent\".  Considering that \"percent of what\" is VERY subjective on a fan."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "Just below this in the commit message I've included the longDescription of the Rotational ReadingType enum. Specifically:\n\n>Services should represent fan speed and pump speed sensors with the `ReadingType` value `Percent`.\n\nThis was added to 2025.3\n\nFor comparison the v1_11_0 of Sensor does not contain that statement.\n```\ncurl -s https://redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/Sensor.v1_11_0.json | jq .definitions.ReadingType.enumLongDescriptions.Rotational\n\"This value shall indicate a measurement of rotational frequency, in revolutions per minute units.  The `ReadingUnits` property shall contain either `{rev}/min`, which is preferred, or `RPM`, which is a deprecated value.\"\n```\n\nThis Redfish change was after questions we had on the implementation of SpeedRPM with fan sensors. It was discussed in review comment: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/73700/comments/deae0bcb_0c7ce4e2\n\nIs the enum definition not sufficient in the commit message?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "https://github.com/DMTF/Redfish/issues/6197 is the Redfish issue"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "I've added the links to the Redfish issue and PR with changes for the issue."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Great, that's much better documentation, and now the commit message is self sufficient to describe the change."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Reopening, still need some amount of description of what the user facing upshot is.  \"X property is removed, replaced with Y property, and X property changes to Rotational\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "I've added summary of difference which will be reflected in response to the commit message. I've also added an example of the unchanged response for clarity."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This seems like it states the opposite of what you're implementing?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "My reading of the description is that for non fan speed and pump speed sensors that use Rotational they would use the rev/min or RPM for the ReadingUnits.\n\nBut for the exception cases of fan speed and pump speed sensors they should not be using Rotational at all."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't think this part is important.. Maybe just remove it and go with the last sentence? Which is the new sentence here.."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
