                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "I've reworded to reference just the added sentence for clarity of why this change is being introduced."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 337,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Should we plan to disable first ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 337,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "Good point! Updating to default to disabled January 2027 with complete removal by June 2027."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/sensor_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 486,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Why are we unpacking the properties AGAIN?  There's already an unpack of these properties in the code you've added this to."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/sensor_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 486,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "The unpack of these properties is a single one at a time and direct assignment into the JSON. But all three are needed at one time in order to calculate the percent. We also separately unpack properties for determing the Health/Status in the objectPropertiesToJson() function."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/sensor_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 486,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "I've restructured the flow here and rebased on top of the restructure of objectPropertiesToJson().\n\nNow:\n fillSensorIdentity() will unpack these values as well and pass down to new function convertToFanPercent() to do the conversion work. (I'm keeping a separate getFanPercent() function for unit testing and for eventual use by ThermalMetrics which is not an excerpt, so has different Redfish property names for the same information.)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/sensor_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 527,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "No, that's not how this works.  if min value isn't published, we either don't publish the property at all or we mark it null."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/sensor_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 527,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "Modified to match how missing maxValue is handled, so the property won't be published if we cannot compute the percent."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/sensor_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 537,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Divide by zero safety issue."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/sensor_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 537,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "range is computed and checked at L531 above. If it is <= 0 we will return and not do this division."
                },
                {
